5,1,1,talk,Minato,,I wonder who actually does the extra work when a project starts.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
6,1,1,talk,Jonathan,,I’m concerned about the external conditions we assume are stable. Who verifies access at customer plants before we commit to a timeline?,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
7,1,1,talk,George,,I worry about the hidden costs. Who checks if the capital budget actually covers the renewal fees that arrive next year?,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
8,1,1,talk,May,,I’m curious about the ghosts in the machine. Who checks if we’re just repeating the same mistakes from last year’s winners?,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
9,1,1,talk,Midori,,"I’m worried we judge by how impressive things sound, not what actually breaks on the floor. Who tracks the weekly losses?","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
10,1,2,talk,Minato,,I think we should look at the staffing of the coordination group. It seems important to know who is actually there to help.,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
11,1,2,talk,Jonathan,,I’d like to verify the network coverage at customer plants. We can’t promise timelines if we don’t know if the connection actually exists.,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
12,1,2,talk,George,,I need to see the capital budget and software allowance. The renewal notice is where the real bill hides.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
13,1,2,talk,May,,"I want to see the outcomes of the last three internal rollouts. We need to know what actually survived, not just what sounded good.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
14,1,2,talk,Midori,,"I’d like to examine the misrouted deliveries in the incident logs. I need to see the real, weekly friction on the floor.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
15,1,3,talk,Minato,,I’m still thinking about the coordination group. Maybe I should also look at how vendor queries are handled?,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
16,1,3,talk,Jonathan,,"I’ll also check in-house developer availability. If the hands aren’t free, the timeline is fiction.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
17,1,3,talk,George,,I’ll also examine the vendor licence pricing versus fixed-fee work. I need to know if we’re buying a trap or a tool.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
18,1,3,talk,May,,"I’ll also check the record of cross-unit standardization efforts. If we keep reinventing the wheel, that’s the pattern I need to expose.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
19,1,3,talk,Midori,,I’ll also look at the time lost to copying existing records. That’s the silent tax on our daily effort.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
20,1,4,talk,Minato,,I’ll stick with my two choices. I want to see who is really there to help and how we handle the questions.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
21,1,4,talk,Jonathan,,I’ll stick with my two choices. Verifying the connection and the hands is the only way to ground our promises in reality.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
22,1,4,talk,George,,I’ll stick with my two choices. The renewal notice is where the real bill hides. I need to see the true cost before we commit.,"{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
23,1,4,talk,May,,I’ll stick with my two choices. The past is the only honest witness. I need to see if we’re just repeating the same mistakes.,"{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
24,1,4,talk,Midori,,"I’ll stick with my two choices. I need to see the real, weekly friction and the silent tax on our daily effort.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
