35,2,1,talk,Minato,,I found that only two people write all the notes by hand. That seems very heavy for just them.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Jonathan,,"The data is sobering. Half the sites lose signal afternoons, and approval took six weeks. My developers are locked until Q3. We cannot promise timelines on this foundation.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,George,,"The capital line is frozen, but the software allowance has room. However, per-head licences climb with every department added. Fixed-fee work is stable.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,May,,"My findings are stark. Broad, daily-entry tools get abandoned; narrow, trade-specific ones survive. Standardization efforts mostly die without an owner. We keep repeating this.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Midori,,"The logs show eleven misrouted deliveries, all from duplicate addresses. Meanwhile, we lose an hour daily copying records. That’s the real friction we must solve.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Minato,,"@Midori, that sounds exhausting. If we are copying records all day, who has time to actually fix the problems?","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Jonathan,,"@Minato, the copying is a symptom. The real bottleneck is the six-week approval and missing signal. We cannot build on that.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,George,,"@Jonathan, the frozen capital line means we cannot fund new per-head licences. We must choose a fixed-fee solution to avoid next year’s renewal trap.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,May,,"@George, fixed-fee is smart, but my data shows narrow tools survive. We need a solution that fits one trade, not a bloated platform everyone abandons.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Midori,,"@May, I agree. Narrow tools survive because they respect the daily rhythm. We must avoid bloated platforms that just add more copying to our already heavy workload.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Minato,,"@May, I agree. If the tools are too big, people stop using them. I worry the two people writing notes will just get more tired.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Jonathan,,"@May, precisely. A narrow tool respects the six-week approval delay. We must avoid anything requiring broad, unstable network access at those half-connected sites.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,George,,"@Jonathan, I agree. But a fixed-fee build is only safe if it doesn’t trigger a capital request. We must stay within the software allowance to avoid the frozen line.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,May,,"@George, exactly. The software allowance is our lifeline. We must pick a narrow, fixed-fee tool that fits one trade, avoiding the capital trap entirely.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Midori,,"@George, I agree. We must stay within the software allowance. A narrow, fixed-fee tool respects our budget and the daily rhythm, avoiding the capital trap entirely.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Minato,,"@George, I agree. We must protect the two people writing notes. A simple, fixed-fee tool helps them breathe. I hope we choose wisely.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Jonathan,,"@George, agreed. We must stay within the software allowance. A narrow, fixed-fee tool respects the budget and the reality of our disconnected sites.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,George,,"@Minato, I agree. We must avoid the renewal trap. A fixed-fee build within the software allowance is the only path that respects our frozen capital line.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,May,,"@Minato, I agree. We must protect those two note-takers. A narrow, fixed-fee tool respects their rhythm and avoids the capital trap. Let’s choose wisely.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Midori,,"@Minato, I agree. We must protect those two note-takers. A narrow, fixed-fee tool respects their rhythm and avoids the capital trap. Let’s choose wisely.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
